    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 05)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, serial multi-part narrative arcs, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network broadcasting history (1936–1950):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 05)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Inner_Sanctum_1942_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Dead Man&#39;s Magic</code>, <code>Carter&#39;s Liver Pills 1942</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Dead Man&#39;s Magic (Carter&#39;s Little Liver Pills)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1942-08-23<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Carter Products, Inc.</strong><br>Carter&#39;s Little Liver Pills &amp; Arrid</td>\n<td><strong>Raymond Edward Johnson</strong> (Host), <strong>Paul McGrath</strong>, <strong>Lesley Woods</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Himan Brown</strong> (Creator &amp; Director), <strong>Milton Lewis</strong> (Writer), <strong>Ed Herlihy</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Horror&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Psychological Thriller&quot;, &quot;Supernatural&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Host Raymond opens the squeaking door for a chilling tale of an ambitious stage magician who murders his mentor to steal an ancient Egyptian occult illusion, only to find himself terrorized on stage when the deceased master&#39;s spirit manipulates the deadly guillotine apparatus.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Inner_Sanctum_1948_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Only the Dead Will Know</code>, <code>Bromo-Seltzer 1948</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Only the Dead Will Know (Bromo-Seltzer)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1948-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>The Emerson Drug Co.</strong><br>Bromo-Seltzer (&quot;Fight headache 3 ways&quot;)</td>\n<td><strong>Paul McGrath</strong> (Host), <strong>Everett Sloane</strong>, <strong>Mercedes McCambridge</strong>, <strong>Karl Swenson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Himan Brown</strong> (Director), <strong>John Roeburt</strong> (Writer), <strong>Dwight Weist</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Horror&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Psychological Thriller&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A panicked amnesiac awakens in a blood-spattered hotel suite with a smoking revolver in his coat pocket, desperately retracing his lost steps through midnight streets to prove whether he was framed or if he truly murdered his wealthy business partner.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Man_On_Farm_1947_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Quaker Oats Farm</code>, <code>Ful-O-Pep 1947</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Live from the Quaker Oats Experimental Farm (Ful-O-Pep Feeds)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual / Syndication</strong><br>1947-08-23<br>12:00 PM CST</td>\n<td><strong>Quaker Oats Company</strong><br>Ful-O-Pep Livestock &amp; Poultry Feeds</td>\n<td><strong>Chuck Acree</strong> (MC), <strong>Dr. O.B. Kent</strong>, <strong>Ray Ferris</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Quaker Oats Radio Division</strong>, <strong>Don Wilson</strong> (Sound Engineer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Agriculture&quot;, &quot;Educational&quot;, &quot;Talk&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Master of Ceremonies Chuck Acree broadcasts live from the Quaker Oats Experimental Farm in Libertyville, Illinois, interviewing Midwestern livestock farmers, conducting agricultural quiz contests, and sharing scientific poultry-raising advice for Ful-O-Pep Feeds.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Dr_Christian_1944_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Cupid Is the Villain</code>, <code>Vaseline Hair Tonic 1944</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Cupid Is the Villain (Vaseline Brand Products)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1944-08-23<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Chesebrough Mfg. Co.</strong><br>Vaseline Petroleum Jelly &amp; Hair Tonic</td>\n<td><strong>Jean Hersholt</strong> (Dr. Christian), <strong>Rosemary DeCamp</strong> (Judy), <strong>Art Gilmore</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ruth Adams Knight</strong> (Writer), <strong>Dorothy McCann</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Medical&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Small Town&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Beloved country physician Dr. Paul Christian and loyal nurse Judy Price intervene when a well-meaning but meddlesome River&#39;s End town matchmaker nearly destroys the engagement of a returning wounded soldier and his high-school sweetheart.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Dr_Christian_1950_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Top Dog</code>, <code>River&#39;s End Dog Show 1950</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Top Dog (The River&#39;s End Dog Show)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1950-08-23<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Chesebrough Mfg. Co.</strong><br>Vaseline Brand Products</td>\n<td><strong>Jean Hersholt</strong> (Dr. Christian), <strong>Rosemary DeCamp</strong> (Judy), <strong>Parley Baer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ruth Adams Knight</strong> (Writer), <strong>Dorothy McCann</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Medical&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Small Town&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Dr. Paul Christian helps an eccentric local kennel owner enter his champion terrier into the county fair dog show, overcoming a wealthy rival&#39;s underhanded scheme to disqualify the beloved community pup.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Green_Hornet_1936_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Part 1 of 3</code>, <code>Protection Racket Serial</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Political Protection Racket (Part 1)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>WXYZ / Mutual</strong><br>1936-08-23<br>7:30 PM EST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Selected Regional Advertisers</td>\n<td><strong>Al Hodge</strong> (Britt Reid / Green Hornet), <strong>Raymond Hayashi</strong> (Kato), <strong>Lenore Allman</strong></td>\n<td><strong>George W. Trendle &amp; Fran Striker</strong> (Creators), <strong>James Jewell</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 1 of a three-part serial adventure, crusading <em>Daily Sentinel</em> publisher Britt Reid and his confidant Kato don their masks and board the Black Beauty to infiltrate a ruthless municipal protection racket shaking down waterfront merchants.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 30</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
