    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 04)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network, public, and syndication broadcasting history (1943–1998):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 04)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>WFUV_1998_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Big Broadcast Parts 3 And 4</code>, <code>Rich Conaty WFUV 1998</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Big Broadcast: Rich Conaty with 1920s &amp; 1930s Jazz 78s (Hours 3 &amp; 4)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>WFUV 90.7 FM</strong><br>1998-08-23<br>8:00 PM</td>\n<td><strong>Member-supported</strong><br>WFUV Fordham University</td>\n<td><strong>Rich Conaty</strong> (Host &amp; Jazz Historian)</td>\n<td><strong>Rich Conaty</strong> (Producer), WFUV Studios, Bronx, NY</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Jazz&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Renowned vintage jazz host Rich Conaty presents hours three and four of <em>The Big Broadcast</em> from WFUV Fordham University, spinning original 78rpm jazz and dance band pressings from Paul Whiteman, Bix Beiderbecke, and Ruth Etting with archival discographical commentary.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Theater_Romance_1943_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Lady Hamilton</code>, <code>Romance Halo Shampoo 1943</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Lady Hamilton (Starring Madeleine Carroll &amp; Brian Aherne)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1943-08-23<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Colgate-Palmolive-Peet</strong><br>Colgate Dental Cream &amp; Halo</td>\n<td><strong>Madeleine Carroll</strong> (Lady Hamilton), <strong>Brian Aherne</strong> (Lord Nelson), <strong>Ian Keith</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jean Holloway</strong> (Writer), <strong>Charles Martin</strong> (Director), <strong>Frank Gallop</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Madeleine Carroll and Brian Aherne star in a passionate dramatization of the legendary wartime romance between Lady Emma Hamilton and British naval hero Lord Horatio Nelson against the backdrop of the Napoleonic Wars.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Guest_Star_1953_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Hayes Versus Hayes</code>, <code>Peter Lind Hayes Mary Healy</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Guest Star #335: Peter Lind Hayes &amp; Mary Healy in &#39;Hayes vs. Hayes&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Treasury Syndication</strong><br>1953-08-23<br>(Guest Star #335)</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Treasury Dept.</strong><br>U.S. Savings Bonds</td>\n<td><strong>Peter Lind Hayes</strong>, <strong>Mary Healy</strong>, <strong>Ray Bloch and Treasury Orchestra</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Warren Somerville</strong> (Director), <strong>Rex Marshall</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Public Affairs&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Husband-and-wife comedy duo Peter Lind Hayes and Mary Healy present witty domestic squabbles, song parodies, and musical duets to promote United States Savings Bonds for the Treasury Department.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Guest_Star_1959_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Yours In Song</code>, <code>Gisele MacKenzie Buddy Cole</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Guest Star #648: Gisele MacKenzie Sings &#39;Yours in Song&#39; with Buddy Cole&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Treasury Syndication</strong><br>1959-08-23<br>(Guest Star #648)</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Treasury Dept.</strong><br>U.S. Savings Bonds</td>\n<td><strong>Gisele MacKenzie</strong>, <strong>Buddy Cole and his Orchestra</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Buddy Cole</strong> (Arranger), <strong>Jack O&#39;Brian</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;, &quot;Public Affairs&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Singing star Gisele MacKenzie performs a sparkling set of Broadway standards and pop ballads including &#39;Yours in Song&#39; alongside Buddy Cole&#39;s swinging studio orchestra, encouraging Americans to invest in U.S. Savings Bonds.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Guest_Star_1964_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Bluesette</code>, <code>Toots Thielemans Dick Hyman</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Guest Star #909: Toots Thielemans Plays &#39;Bluesette&#39; with Dick Hyman&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Treasury Syndication</strong><br>1964-08-23<br>(Guest Star #909)</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Treasury Dept.</strong><br>U.S. Savings Bonds</td>\n<td><strong>Toots Thielemans</strong> (Harmonica &amp; Guitar), <strong>Dick Hyman Rhythm Trio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Malcolm Addey</strong> (Audio Engineer), <strong>Dan Ingram</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Jazz&quot;, &quot;Instrumental&quot;, &quot;Public Affairs&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Virtuoso jazz harmonicist and guitarist Toots Thielemans performs his signature jazz waltz masterpiece &#39;Bluesette&#39; alongside pianist Dick Hyman, delivering public service appeals for United States Savings Bonds.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Mystery_Theater_1949_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Dream Girl Murder</code>, <code>Inspector Hearthstone Bayer</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Inspector Hearthstone of the Yard: The Dream Girl Murder Case (Bayer Aspirin)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1949-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sterling Drug, Inc.</strong><br>Bayer Aspirin &amp; Phillips&#39; Milk of Magnesia</td>\n<td><strong>Alfred Shirley</strong> (Hearthstone), <strong>James Monks</strong> (Sam Cook), <strong>Mercedes McCambridge</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Frank Gould</strong> (Writer), <strong>Frank Telford</strong> (Director), <strong>Ken Roberts</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Inspector Hearthstone of Scotland Yard investigates the poisoning of a celebrated Broadway model and glamour girl inside her luxury duplex penthouse, deducing that the lethal dose of aconite was concealed inside a sealed jar of cold cream.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 24</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
