    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 01)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch initiates the sequential archival walk for <strong>August 23rd</strong>, documenting the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on August 23 across American and British broadcasting history (1943–1986):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 01)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Sea_Hound_1943_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Pearl Smugglers Galapagos</code>, <code>Captain Silver 1943</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Pearl Smugglers of the Galápagos&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1943-08-23<br>5:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>CIAA / Non-commercial</strong><br>Inter-American Affairs</td>\n<td><strong>Ken Daigneau</strong> (Captain Silver), <strong>Bobby Hastings</strong> (Jerry), <strong>Alan Devitt</strong> (Kukua)</td>\n<td><strong>Fran Striker &amp; Martin Andrews</strong> (Writers), <strong>Cyril Armbrister</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Children&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Maritime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Captain Silver and youthful first mate Jerry navigate the diesel schooner <em>Sea Hound</em> into a volcanic cove off the Galápagos Islands, outmaneuvering a syndicate of Axis pearl smugglers who established a clandestine shortwave radio transmission bunker.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Kay_Kyser_1944_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Swinging On A Star</code>, <code>Kay Kyser Colgate 1944</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Kay Kyser: &#39;Swinging on a Star&#39; &amp; Musical Knowledge Quiz (Colgate)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1944-08-23<br>8:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Colgate-Palmolive-Peet</strong><br>Colgate Dental Cream &amp; Palmolive</td>\n<td><strong>Kay Kyser</strong> (The Ol&#39; Professor), <strong>Georgia Carroll</strong>, <strong>Ish Kabibble</strong>, <strong>Harry Babbitt</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bud Freeman &amp; Ed Haldeman</strong> (Writers), <strong>Frank O&#39;Connor</strong> (Director), <strong>Verne Smith</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Quiz&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Ol&#39; Professor Kay Kyser puts serviceman contestants through their musical paces on the Kollege quiz, featuring Ish Kabibble&#39;s zany comedy poems and Georgia Carroll leading the band in the chart-topping hit &#39;Swinging on a Star&#39; for Colgate Dental Cream.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Curtain_Time_1947_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Peach For Professor</code>, <code>Curtain Time Milky Way</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;A Peach for the Professor (Sponsored by Mars Candy Bars)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WMAQ)</strong><br>1947-08-23<br>7:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Mars, Incorporated</strong><br>Milky Way, Snickers &amp; Mars Bars</td>\n<td><strong>Harry Elders</strong>, <strong>Nanette Sargent</strong>, <strong>Donald Gallagher</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mike Wallace &amp; Russell Maloney</strong> (Writers), <strong>Norman Felton</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A flustered, bookish university botany professor finds his tranquil bachelor life turned upside down when a vivacious Hollywood starlet arrives in town to study rare orchids for an upcoming film role and moves next door.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ISIHAC_1986_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Caterers Ball</code>, <code>Series 14 Ep 6 Clue</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;I&#39;m Sorry I Haven&#39;t a Clue: &#39;Caterers Ball&#39; (Series 14, Episode 6)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1986-08-23<br>12:27 PM</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>British Broadcasting Corp.</td>\n<td><strong>Humphrey Lyttelton</strong> (Chair), <strong>Barry Cryer</strong>, <strong>Graeme Garden</strong>, <strong>Tim Brooke-Taylor</strong>, <strong>Willie Rushton</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Graeme Garden</strong> (Creator), <strong>Paul Mayhew-Archer</strong> (Producer), <strong>Colin Sell</strong> (Piano)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Satire&quot;, &quot;Panel Game&quot;, &quot;Improvisation&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Chairman Humphrey Lyttelton presides over the antidote to panel games as regulars Barry Cryer, Graeme Garden, Tim Brooke-Taylor, and Willie Rushton compete in &#39;One Song to the Tune of Another&#39; (including singing &#39;Caterers Ball&#39;) and a contentious round of Mornington Crescent.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Cities_Service_1954_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Band of America</code>, <code>Highways in Melody 1954</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Paul Lavalle and the Cities Service Band of America&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1954-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Cities Service Oil Co.</strong><br>Cities Service Gasoline &amp; Koolmotor</td>\n<td><strong>Paul Lavalle and Band of America</strong>, <strong>Green Brothers Marimba Ensemble</strong>, <strong>Quartet</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Paul Lavalle</strong> (Producer &amp; Conductor), <strong>Ford Bond</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Classical&quot;, &quot;Brass Band&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Maestro Paul Lavalle conducts the forty-eight piece Cities Service Band of America through stirring renditions of John Philip Sousa marches, American show tunes, and a virtuoso marimba arrangement of &#39;Flight of the Bumblebee&#39; for Cities Service Gasoline.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Confession_1953_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>James V Madsen Case</code>, <code>Armed Robbery Confession</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The James V. Madsen Case (Armed Bank Robbery Confession)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1953-08-23<br>9:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Crime Documentary</td>\n<td><strong>Donald MacDonald</strong> (Narrator / Interviewer), dramatic cast &amp; prison recordings</td>\n<td><strong>Howard Blake</strong> (Writer), <strong>Warren Lewis</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Documentary&quot;, &quot;True Crime&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Legal&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Real-life tape-recorded prison interviews and dramatic reenactments document the criminal downfall of James V. Madsen, a young war veteran whose escalating gambling debts led him to commit a series of desperate armed bank robberies across Northern California.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
