    "html": "<h2>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for 6 historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 22</strong> across British and American dramatic broadcasting history (1959–1999):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Inventory</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Ware_Case_1959_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Ware Case</code>, <code>Sir Hubert Ware Trial</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Ware Case (Starring Michael Denison &amp; Dulcie Gray)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Home Service</strong><br>1959-08-22<br>8:30 PM</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>British Broadcasting Corp.</td>\n<td><strong>Michael Denison</strong> (Sir Gerald Loddon), <strong>Dulcie Gray</strong>, <strong>Derek Blomfield</strong>, <strong>Brewster Mason</strong></td>\n<td><strong>George Pleydell Bancroft</strong> (Playwright), <strong>Cynthia Pughe</strong> (Adapter), <strong>Archie Campbell</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Legal&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Theatre&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Eminent barrister Sir Gerald Loddon defends his charming, aristocratic brother-in-law Sir Hubert Ware at the Old Bailey against charges of drowning his wealthy young brother-in-law, securing an acquittal before an agonizing private confession shatters the family.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Trustee_Toolroom_1964_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Trustee from Toolroom</code>, <code>Nevil Shute Adaptation</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Trustee from the Toolroom (by Nevil Shute, Starring Cyril Shaps)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Home Service</strong><br>1964-08-22<br>8:30 PM</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>British Broadcasting Corp.</td>\n<td><strong>Cyril Shaps</strong> (Keith Stewart), <strong>Anthony Jacobs</strong>, <strong>Ralph Truman</strong>, <strong>Gudrun Ure</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Nevil Shute</strong> (Author), <strong>Stephen Grenfell</strong> (Adapter), <strong>John Gibson</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Maritime&quot;, &quot;Literature&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Mild-mannered model engineer Keith Stewart embarks on an extraordinary journey from London to a remote Polynesian coral reef to recover twenty-six thousand pounds in miniature diamonds embedded in a sunken yacht for his orphaned niece.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Hornblower_Crisis_1970_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Hornblower and Crisis</code>, <code>CS Forester Trafalgar</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Hornblower and the Crisis (by C.S. Forester, Starring Ray Brooks &amp; Patrick Troughton)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1970-08-22<br>8:30 PM</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>British Broadcasting Corp.</td>\n<td><strong>Ray Brooks</strong> (Horatio Hornblower), <strong>Patrick Troughton</strong> (Meadows), <strong>Anthony Jackson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>C.S. Forester</strong> (Author), <strong>John Keir Cross</strong> (Adapter), <strong>Brian Miller</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Maritime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>During the Napoleonic Wars, Captain Horatio Hornblower is temporarily relieved of his command of the sloop Hotspur to undertake a covert intelligence mission for the British Admiralty, delivering forged French naval orders to mislead Admiral Villeneuve&#39;s fleet before Trafalgar.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Goodbye_Old_Friend_1981_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Goodbye to Old Friend</code>, <code>Brian Freemantle Defector</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Goodbye to an Old Friend (by Brian Freemantle, Starring John Woodvine &amp; Kenneth Cranham)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1981-08-22<br>8:30 PM</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>British Broadcasting Corp.</td>\n<td><strong>John Woodvine</strong> (Chris McCreedy), <strong>Kenneth Cranham</strong> (Viktor), <strong>Sean Arnold</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Brian Freemantle</strong> (Author), <strong>David Buck</strong> (Adapter), <strong>Christopher Venning</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Espionage&quot;, &quot;Thriller&quot;, &quot;Cold War&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Elite British intelligence interrogator Chris McCreedy is tasked with debriefing an extraordinarily high-ranking Soviet aerospace defector in a remote countryside safe house, suspecting that the defector&#39;s valuable scientific revelations are a plant designed to compromise Western satellite defenses.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Unto_The_Grave_1987_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Unto the Grave</code>, <code>Canadian Prairie Feud</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Unto the Grave (Starring Robert Beatty &amp; Michael Shannon)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1987-08-22<br>7:45 PM</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>British Broadcasting Corp.</td>\n<td><strong>Robert Beatty</strong> (Ebenezer Jordan), <strong>Michael Shannon</strong> (Jesse), <strong>Elizabeth Bell</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arthur Kelly</strong> (Writer), <strong>Jane Morgan</strong> (Producer &amp; Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>An intense generational drama set on the harsh Canadian prairie frontier where an unyielding pioneer patriarch&#39;s obsession with land ownership drives his sons to rebellion, culminating in a tragic boundary dispute with neighboring homesteaders.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Harry_Nile_1999_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Amazon House</code>, <code>Harry Nile Crisis 1999</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Adventures of Harry Nile: Crisis at Amazon House&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Imagination Theatre</strong><br>1999-08-22<br>(Syndicated)</td>\n<td><strong>National Syndication</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Phil Harper</strong> (Harry Nile), <strong>Pat French</strong> (Murphy), <strong>John Gilbert</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jim French</strong> (Writer &amp; Director), <strong>Terry Rose</strong> (Music)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Seattle private investigator Harry Nile uncovers a treacherous extortion scheme inside Amazon House, an upscale women&#39;s residential club where a wealthy boarder&#39;s mysterious death is revealed to be premeditated poison rather than natural heart failure.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 22</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 22</strong>: 218</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
