    "html": "<h2>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for 6 historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 22</strong> across American, Australian, and military broadcasting history (1937–1951):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Inventory</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>The_Fat_Man_1947_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>TCOT Phony Medium</code>, <code>Brad Runyon Pepto-Bismol</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Phony Medium&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1947-08-22<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Norwich Pharmacal Co.</strong><br>Pepto-Bismol &amp; Unguentine</td>\n<td><strong>J. Scott Smart</strong> (Brad Runyon), <strong>Ed Begley</strong> (Lt. O&#39;Hara), <strong>Robert Sloane</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Dashiell Hammett</strong> (Creator), <strong>Lawrence Klee</strong> (Writer), <strong>Charles Powers</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Brad Runyon steps onto the weighing scale before investigating a fraudulent spiritualist medium who bilked a grieving wealthy client out of tens of thousands of dollars, cornering the psychic blackmailer when the medium&#39;s assistant turns up murdered behind the parlor curtains.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Fat_Man_1951_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Golden Idol</code>, <code>Sydney Harbor Homicide</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Golden Idol (Sydney Harbor Homicide)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Grace Gibson Syndication</strong><br>1951-08-22<br>(2UE Sydney)</td>\n<td><strong>Regional Advertisers</strong><br>Australian Syndication</td>\n<td><strong>Max Osbiston</strong> (Brad Runyon), <strong>Peter Bathurst</strong> (Faraday), <strong>Lyndall Barbour</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Dashiell Hammett</strong> (Creator), <strong>Grace Gibson</strong> (Director), <strong>John Appleton</strong> (Sound)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Sydney, 240-pound private investigator Brad Runyon probes the dockside murder of a marine salvage captain, uncovering an international jewel smuggling ring that smuggled antique golden idols from Southeast Asia inside hollowed ship timber.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Bob_Hope_1937_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Peaches and Cream</code>, <code>Woodbury Rippling Rhythm</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Peaches and Cream Melodrama with Shep Fields&#39; Orchestra (Woodbury&#39;s Soap)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1937-08-22<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Andrew Jergens Co.</strong><br>Woodbury&#39;s Facial Soap (&quot;Skin you love to touch&quot;)</td>\n<td><strong>Bob Hope</strong> (MC), <strong>Shep Fields Orchestra</strong>, <strong>Frank Parker</strong> (Tenor), <strong>Honeychile Wilder</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bob Hope</strong> (Writer), <strong>Monte Brice</strong> (Director), <strong>Jimmy Wallington</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Master of Ceremonies Bob Hope delivers rapid-fire one-liners and parodies Broadway opening nights with a spoof melodrama titled &#39;Peaches and Cream&#39;, backed by Shep Fields&#39; bubbling Rippling Rhythm clarinet and tenor Frank Parker for Woodbury&#39;s Soap.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Murder_Clinic_1943_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Absolute Zero</code>, <code>Cold Storage Murders</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Absolute Zero (The Cold Storage Laboratory Murder)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1943-08-22<br>10:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Mystery Series</td>\n<td><strong>Ronald Dawson</strong> (Dr. John Bent), <strong>James Monks</strong>, <strong>Santos Ortega</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Walter Lurie</strong> (Director), <strong>Jack Amerine</strong> (Sound Effects), <strong>Frank Waldecker</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Criminologist Dr. John Bent investigates an impossible locked-room murder inside a temperature-controlled laboratory cold-storage vault where a brilliant refrigeration engineer was found frozen to absolute zero despite the heating thermostat being turned to high.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Jubilee_1947_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>AFRS Jubilee 272</code>, <code>Count Basie Jack Paar</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;AFRS Jubilee #272: Count Basie Orchestra with Jack Paar &amp; Margaret Whiting&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRS Transcription</strong><br>1947-08-22<br>(NBC Hollywood)</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>Armed Forces Radio Service</td>\n<td><strong>Ernie Whitman</strong> (MC), <strong>Jack Paar</strong>, <strong>Margaret Whiting</strong>, <strong>Count Basie Orchestra</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRS Los Angeles</strong>, <strong>Bud Pollard</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Jazz&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Military&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Master of Ceremonies Ernie &#39;Bubbles&#39; Whitman welcomes guest comedian Jack Paar and vocalist Margaret Whiting to AFRS Jubilee, featuring Count Basie and his Orchestra tearing through swinging jazz classics for Allied servicemen worldwide.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Aldrich_Family_1940_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Cross Country Road Trip</code>, <code>Henry Jalopy 1940</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Henry and Homer Start Their Cross-Country Road Trip&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1940-08-22<br>8:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>General Foods Corp.</strong><br>Jell-O Gelatin &amp; Puddings</td>\n<td><strong>Ezra Stone</strong> (Henry Aldrich), <strong>Jackie Kelk</strong> (Homer Brown), <strong>House Jameson</strong>, <strong>Katharine Raht</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Clifford Goldsmith</strong> (Creator), <strong>Bob Welch</strong> (Director), <strong>Harry von Zell</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Teens&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Henry Aldrich and best pal Homer Brown attempt to embark on an ambitious cross-country summer road trip in a rebuilt second-hand jalopy, causing utter pandemonium across Centerville when their exhaust backfires through Mr. Aldrich&#39;s flowerbeds.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 22</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 22</strong>: 200</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
