    "html": "<h2>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for 6 historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 22</strong> across American network broadcasting history (1943–1960):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Inventory</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Lands_Free_1943_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>A A Berle Speaker</code>, <code>Inter-American Unity</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Assistant Secretary of State Adolf A. Berle Jr. on Post-War Inter-American Unity&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1943-08-22<br>4:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>NBC University</strong><br>Inter-American Cultural Air</td>\n<td><strong>Adolf A. Berle Jr.</strong> (Keynote Speaker), dramatic cast</td>\n<td><strong>Sterling Fisher</strong> (Director), <strong>Ranald MacDougall</strong> (Writer), <strong>Frank Blair</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Educational&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Talk&quot;, &quot;Public Affairs&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Assistant Secretary of State Adolf A. Berle Jr. addresses the NBC Inter-American University of the Air, outlining the Roosevelt administration&#39;s Good Neighbor policy and articulating how cooperative hemispheric defense and trade pacts will preserve democratic sovereignty after World War II.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Meet_Miss_Sherlock_1946_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Counterfeit Pearls</code>, <code>Jane Sherlock 1946</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Counterfeit Cultured Pearls&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1946-08-22<br>10:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Summer Mystery</td>\n<td><strong>Monty Margetts</strong> (Jane Sherlock), <strong>Bill Conrad</strong> (Peter Blossom), <strong>Joe Forte</strong></td>\n<td><strong>E. Jack Neuman</strong> (Writer), <strong>David Vaile</strong> (Director), <strong>Doug Gourlay</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Keen-eyed patent law secretary Jane Sherlock drags her frustrated police detective boyfriend Peter Blossom into the Manhattan diamond district when a wealthy socialite&#39;s insurance claim exposes an elaborate syndicate swapping genuine cultured pearls for glass duplicates.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Bing_Crosby_1955_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Bing and Marilyn Maxwell</code>, <code>Bing Crosby GE 1955</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Bing Crosby with Guest Marilyn Maxwell &amp; The Buddy Cole Trio&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (KNX / WCBS)</strong><br>1955-08-22<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Electric</strong><br>GE Appliances &amp; Telechron Clocks</td>\n<td><strong>Bing Crosby</strong>, <strong>Marilyn Maxwell</strong> (Guest Vocalist), <strong>Buddy Cole Trio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bill Morrow</strong> (Writer), <strong>Murdo MacKenzie</strong> (Director), <strong>Ken Carpenter</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Der Bingle exchanges easygoing banter with guest singer Marilyn Maxwell and croons timeless American standards backed by Buddy Cole&#39;s intimate jazz trio, performing &#39;Learning the Blues&#39;, &#39;Something&#39;s Gotta Give&#39;, and &#39;Love and Marriage&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Bing_Crosby_1956_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Bing Cathy Crosby</code>, <code>Cool Cool Evening Ford</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Bing and Cathy Crosby Sing &#39;In the Cool, Cool, Cool of the Evening&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (KNX)</strong><br>1956-08-22<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Ford Motor Company</strong><br>Ford Division</td>\n<td><strong>Bing Crosby</strong>, <strong>Cathy Crosby</strong> (Guest Vocalist), <strong>Buddy Cole Trio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bill Morrow</strong> (Writer), <strong>Murdo MacKenzie</strong> (Director), <strong>Ken Carpenter</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Bing Crosby welcomes his talented niece Cathy Crosby to the microphone for playful family duets and relaxed summer listening, performing &#39;In the Cool, Cool, Cool of the Evening&#39; and &#39;True Love&#39; with Buddy Cole&#39;s rhythms for Ford.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Bing_Crosby_1958_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Laughing Eddie Upjohn</code>, <code>Bing Crosby 1958</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Bing Crosby and &#39;Laughing&#39; Eddie Upjohn&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (KNX)</strong><br>1958-08-22<br>7:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Radio Network</td>\n<td><strong>Bing Crosby</strong>, <strong>Eddie Upjohn</strong> (Comedian), <strong>Buddy Cole and his Rhythm</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bill Morrow</strong> (Writer), <strong>Murdo MacKenzie</strong> (Director), <strong>Ken Carpenter</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Bing Crosby jokes with eccentric comedic monologist &#39;Laughing&#39; Eddie Upjohn between effortless vocal stylings backed by Buddy Cole&#39;s quartet, singing &#39;Volare (Nel Blu Dipinto Di Blu)&#39; and &#39;Gigi&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Bing_Crosby_1960_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Cheek To Cheek</code>, <code>Bing and Rosie 1960</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Bing Crosby &amp; Rosemary Clooney: &#39;Cheek to Cheek&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1960-08-22<br>10:45 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Daytime CBS Radio Network</td>\n<td><strong>Bing Crosby</strong>, <strong>Rosemary Clooney</strong>, <strong>Buddy Cole and his Trio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bill Morrow</strong> (Writer), <strong>Murdo MacKenzie</strong> (Director), <strong>Ken Carpenter</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Bing Crosby and Rosemary Clooney harmonize in relaxed 1960 daytime broadcasting, opening with Irving Berlin&#39;s classic &#39;Cheek to Cheek&#39; and trading sparkling witty banter alongside piano arrangements by Buddy Cole.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 22</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 22</strong>: 182</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
