    "html": "<h2>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for 6 historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 22</strong> across American network and syndicated broadcasting history (1935–1946):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Inventory</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Death_Valley_Days_1935_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Mark Twain Duel</code>, <code>Virginia City 1864</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Mark Twain Fights a Duel in Virginia City&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1935-08-22<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Pacific Coast Borax Co.</strong><br>20 Mule Team Borax &amp; Boraxo</td>\n<td><strong>Tim Frawley</strong> (The Old Ranger), <strong>Jack MacBryde</strong>, <strong>John White</strong> (Lonesome Cowboy)</td>\n<td><strong>Ruth Cornwall Woodman</strong> (Writer), <strong>Edwin M. Whitney</strong> (Director), <strong>George Hicks</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Old Ranger recounts the hilarious historical incident in 1864 Virginia City when young newspaperman Samuel Clemens (Mark Twain) gets challenged to a deadly pistol duel by a rival editor, bluffing his way out of the showdown by shooting the head off a bird with the help of his quick-thinking second.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Death_Valley_Days_1941_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Ghost Great White Sands</code>, <code>New Mexico Mirage</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Ghost of the Great White Sands&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1941-08-22<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Pacific Coast Borax Co.</strong><br>20 Mule Team Borax Flakes</td>\n<td><strong>Harry Humphrey</strong> (The Old Ranger), <strong>Jack MacBryde</strong> (Pioneer Scout), <strong>John White</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ruth Cornwall Woodman</strong> (Writer), <strong>Felix Mills</strong> (Organist), <strong>George Hicks</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Supernatural&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Old Ranger shares the eerie Southwestern legend of a 16th-century Spanish conquistador&#39;s lost bride whose spectral white shroud allegedly drifts across the shimmering gypsum dunes of New Mexico&#39;s White Sands to guide lost desert travelers toward safety.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Doctor_Fights_1944_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Surgeon on Saipan</code>, <code>Penicillin Under Fire</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Combat Surgeon on Saipan (Starring Walter Pidgeon)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1944-08-22<br>9:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Schenley Laboratories</strong><br>Penicillin-Schenley</td>\n<td><strong>Walter Pidgeon</strong> (Guest Star Host / Army Combat Surgeon), supporting cast</td>\n<td><strong>Arthur Heinemann</strong> (Writer), <strong>Marx Loeb</strong> (Director), <strong>Leith Stevens</strong> (Music), <strong>Ken Niles</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Medical&quot;, &quot;War&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Hollywood star Walter Pidgeon dramatizes the heroic true story of a U.S. Army combat surgeon operating under continuous mortar bombardment in a makeshift tent hospital on Saipan, using newly mass-produced penicillin to save wounded Marines from fatal gangrene infections.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Finnegan_1946_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Stolen Persian Rug</code>, <code>Hotel Chaos 9</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Missing Persian Rug&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1946-08-22<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Summer Comedy</td>\n<td><strong>Stuart Erwin</strong> (Finnegan), <strong>Florence Lake</strong> (Sister), <strong>Lucien Littlefield</strong> (Mr. Henderson)</td>\n<td><strong>Frank Galen</strong> (Writer), <strong>Thomas Freebairn-Smith</strong> (Director), <strong>Frank Martin</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Bewildered apartment hotel manager Finnegan scrambles to recover an eccentric tenant&#39;s antique Persian rug after accidentally sending it to a municipal auction instead of the dry cleaners, enlisting his scatterbrained sister to outbid rival antique collectors.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Tide_Show_1945_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Tide Show Piano Melodies</code>, <code>Jack Fina Remote</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Jack Fina and His Piano Melodies&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndicated</strong><br>1945-08-22<br>(San Francisco)</td>\n<td><strong>Associated Oil Company</strong><br>Flying A Gasoline &amp; Tide Water Oil</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Fina and his Piano Orchestra</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Associated Oil Radio Division</strong>, <strong>Scott Douglas</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Pianist Jack Fina and his orchestra entertain listeners with sparkling cocktail piano arrangements of &#39;Bumble Boogie&#39;, &#39;Dream&#39;, and &#39;Sentimental Journey&#39; for Flying A Gasoline and Tide Water Oil.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Myrt_Marge_1946_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Murder Trial Begins</code>, <code>Backstage Murder Defense</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Backstage Murder Trial Begins&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndicated / Mutual</strong><br>1946-08-22<br>(Transamerican Disc)</td>\n<td><strong>Regional Department Stores</strong><br>Syndicated Retail</td>\n<td><strong>Myrtle Vail</strong> (Myrt), <strong>Helen Mack</strong> (Marge), <strong>Ray Hedge</strong> (Clarence), <strong>Vinton Hayworth</strong> (Jack)</td>\n<td><strong>Myrtle Vail</strong> (Creator &amp; Writer), <strong>Transamerican Broadcasting</strong> (Producers)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;, &quot;Show Business&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>As the sensational backstage murder trial commences, seasoned vaudevillian Myrt takes the witness stand to defend a frightened chorus girl wrongly accused of poisoning a wealthy Broadway producer in his dressing room.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 22</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 22</strong>: 110</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
