    "html": "<h2>Batch 102 Forensic Discoveries</h2>\n<p>Batch 102 recovers and dates 13 archival recordings spanning environmental conservation campaigns, early dramatic work by future science-fiction icons, big band jazz, western comedy variety, Broadway adaptations, and duo-piano mastery: 3 star-studded 1954 U.S. Forest Service conservation programs from <em><strong>Smokey Visits the Stars</strong></em> featuring Bing Crosby, Dinah Shore, and Willard Waterman (<em>The Great Gildersleeve</em>) performing skits and songs with Smokey Bear (voiced by Jackson Weaver), a young DeForest Kelley (future Dr. Leonard &#39;Bones&#39; McCoy in <em>Star Trek</em>) starring in &#39;The Snow Queen&#39; on <em><strong>Stars On Parade</strong></em> alongside Count Basie and His Orchestra (1951), Western character actor Chill Wills hosting his musical variety program with guest Gail Robbins (1952), Rodgers &amp; Hammerstein Broadway scores performed on <em><strong>Theater of Hits</strong></em> including <em>Me and Juliet</em> and <em>Carousel</em> (1953), Sammy Kaye&#39;s famous orchestra broadcasting live from the Steel Pier ballroom in Atlantic City (1942), and duo-piano virtuosos Cy Walter and Walter Gross dueling on <em><strong>Piano Playhouse</strong></em> (1948).</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>Smokey the Bear: Forest Fire Conservation</em> (1954)</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Verified Airdate</th>\n<th>Forest Service Campaign</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Smokey_Bing_Crosby.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Smokey Visits the Stars: Guest Bing Crosby on Forest Fire Prevention&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1954-06-15</strong></td>\n<td>Bing Crosby singing and bantering with Smokey Bear on public forest safety.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Smokey_Dinah_Shore.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Smokey Visits the Stars: Guest Dinah Shore on Wildfire Conservation&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1954-06-22</strong></td>\n<td>Dinah Shore appealing to campers and drivers to extinguish campfires and matches.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Smokey_Willard_Waterman.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Smokey Visits the Stars: Guest Willard Waterman (The Great Gildersleeve)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1954-06-29</strong></td>\n<td>Gildersleeve bringing Summerfield comedy to Smokey Bear&#39;s forest headquarters.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>DeForest Kelley</em>, <em>Count Basie</em>, &amp; <em>Chill Wills</em> (1951–1952)</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Verified Airdate</th>\n<th>Performance / Cast</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>DeForest_Kelley_Snow_Queen.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Stars On Parade: DeForest Kelley in &#39;The Snow Queen&#39; U.S. Army Recruiting Show&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1951-01-14</strong></td>\n<td>Early career dramatic lead by DeForest Kelley years before <em>Star Trek</em>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Count_Basie_Stars_On_Parade.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Stars On Parade: Count Basie and His Orchestra - &#39;Royal Rhythm&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1951-01-21</strong></td>\n<td>Count Basie&#39;s big band swinging for U.S. armed forces recruitment.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Chill_Wills_Gail_Robbins_Pt1.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Chill Wills Show: Guest Singer Gail Robbins &amp; Western Humor (Part 1)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1952-05-18</strong></td>\n<td>Chill Wills spinning cowboy yarns with film actress and singer Gail Robbins.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Chill_Wills_Gail_Robbins_Pt2.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Chill Wills Show: Guest Singer Gail Robbins &amp; Western Humor (Part 2)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1952-05-25</strong></td>\n<td>Part 2 of Chill Wills&#39; western music and comedic banter.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>3. <em>Rodgers &amp; Hammerstein</em>, <em>Sammy Kaye</em>, &amp; <em>Piano Playhouse</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Verified Airdate</th>\n<th>Genre &amp; Production</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Me_And_Juliet_Pt1.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Theater of Hits: Rodgers &amp; Hammerstein&#39;s &#39;Me and Juliet&#39; Starring Isabel Bigley (Part 1)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1953-06-14</strong></td>\n<td>Broadway radio condensation of Rodgers and Hammerstein&#39;s backstage musical.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Me_And_Juliet_Pt2.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Theater of Hits: Rodgers &amp; Hammerstein&#39;s &#39;Me and Juliet&#39; Starring Isabel Bigley (Part 2)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1953-06-21</strong></td>\n<td>The dramatic resolution and score highlights of <em>Me and Juliet</em>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Carousel_John_Raitt.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Theater of Hits: Rodgers &amp; Hammerstein&#39;s &#39;Carousel&#39; Starring John Raitt&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1953-06-28</strong></td>\n<td>John Raitt singing Billy Bigelow&#39;s legendary &#39;Soliloquy&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sammy_Kaye_Steel_Pier.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Swing and Sway with Sammy Kaye: Live from the Steel Pier in Atlantic City&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1942-07-24</strong></td>\n<td>Big band dance remote from New Jersey&#39;s premier seaside ocean pier ballroom.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Piano_Playhouse_Sun_Morning.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Piano Playhouse: Cy Walter &amp; Walter Gross - &#39;I Got the Sun in the Morning&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1948-03-21</strong></td>\n<td>Irving Berlin standard arranged for four hands by Cy Walter and Walter Gross.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Piano_Playhouse_Someone_Watch.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Piano Playhouse: Cy Walter - &#39;Someone to Watch Over Me&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1948-03-28</strong></td>\n<td>Gershwin ballad rendered with Cy Walter&#39;s sophisticated harmonic styling.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n",
