    "markdown": "# Archival Dispatch: 18 Serial Broadcasts Dated Across Aunt Mary and Cecil and Sally\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-21  \n**Author**: radio index  \n**Tags**: Aunt Mary, Cecil and Sally, Daytime Serials, 1930s Radio, Original Filenames, Primary Scans\n\n---\n\n## Batch 10 Forensic Discoveries\n\nBatch 10 resolves 18 historical serialized broadcasts from two of radio's most enduring narrative institutions: the 1942–1943 NBC Pacific Coast master recordings of ***Aunt Mary*** (sponsored by C&H Sugar, written by Gil Doud and Virginia Crosby) and the 1930 San Francisco transcription run of ***Cecil and Sally*** (starring Johnny Patrick and Helen Troy).\n\n---\n\n## 1. *Aunt Mary* — 1942–1943 NBC Pacific Coast Serial Dated\n\nSet in the rural community of Wakefield and Malibu Beach, *Aunt Mary* followed Mary Lane's guidance through wartime family crises:\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Storyline Arc |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Aunt_Mary_Pilot_Story_Of_Aunt_Mary.mp3` | **\"Pilot: The Story of Aunt Mary (C&H Sugar Presentation)\"** | **1942-10-19** | Initial audition pilot introducing Mary Lane and Bill Mead. |\n| `Aunt_Mary_Jessie_Suspicious_Of_Kitt.mp3` | **\"Jessie Suspicious of Kitt's Motives\"** | **1943-03-22** | Bill's loan consultation trip and David Bowman's bank inquiry. |\n| `Aunt_Mary_Jessie_Interrupts_Brett.mp3` | **\"Jessie Interrupts Brett's Luncheon Date\"** | **1943-03-23** | 11th Street confrontation between Jessie Calvert and Brett Cameron. |\n| `Aunt_Mary_Talking_Over_Kitts_Situation.mp3` | **\"Talking Over Kitt's Situation\"** | **1943-03-24** | Bill and Peggy Douglas return from the Wakefield Supper Club. |\n| `Aunt_Mary_Angus_Talks_To_Bill.mp3` | **\"Angus Talks to Bill at the Wakefield Court\"** | **1943-03-25** | Hysterical confrontation at the Wakefield Auto Court. |\n| `Aunt_Mary_Lisa_Learns_Kitt_Pregnant.mp3` | **\"Lisa Learns Kitt Is Pregnant\"** | **1943-03-26** | Sergeant Bill returns from military camp to face marriage disillusionment. |\n| `Aunt_Mary_Kitt_Wants_To_See_Lisa.mp3` | **\"Kitt Wants to See Lisa at Malibu\"** | **1943-03-29** | Living room confrontation with Paul Kramer at Malibu Beach. |\n| `Aunt_Mary_Lisas_Dream.mp3` | **\"Lisa's Malibu Dream\"** | **1943-03-30** | Heavy Pacific fog envelopes the Malibu beach house as dinner is prepared. |\n| `Aunt_Mary_Lisas_Baby_Born.mp3` | **\"Lisa's Baby Born at Malibu Beach\"** | **1943-03-31** | Sunny morning birth at Malibu Beach following dramatic labor. |\n| `Aunt_Mary_DA_Calls_Dr_Larrabee.mp3` | **\"District Attorney Calls Dr. Larrabee at Huntsville\"** | **1943-04-01** | Dr. Martin Larrabee, resident psychiatrist at Huntsville Sanitarium, is summoned. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. *Cecil and Sally* — 1930 San Francisco Master Discs Dated\n\nJohnny Patrick and Helen Troy wrote and voiced this daily 15-minute dialogue comedy for KPO San Francisco:\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Daily Comedy Arc |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Cecil_Sally_Mrs_Mason_Plans_To_Sue.mp3` | **\"Mrs. Mason Plans to Sue Uncle Thomas\"** | **1930-10-27** | Front-page newspaper scandal threatens Uncle Thomas. |\n| `Cecil_Sally_Sally_Has_Cecil_Cut_Hammock.mp3` | **\"Sally Has Cecil Cut the Hammock Strings\"** | **1930-10-28** | Hiding behind the porch drapery during the burning paper scare. |\n| `Cecil_Sally_Gertrude_Mason_Life_Story.mp3` | **\"Gertrude Butterworth Mason Writes Her Life Story\"** | **1930-10-29** | Sally discovers Mrs. Mason's tell-all memoir draft. |\n| `Cecil_Sally_Sally_Turns_Few_Words_Romance.mp3` | **\"Sally Turns a Few Words Into a Deep Romance\"** | **1930-10-30** | Misunderstandings multiply after late-night conversations. |\n| `Cecil_Sally_Willie_Comes_Over.mp3` | **\"Willie Comes Over to Sally's House with Cecil\"** | **1930-10-31** | Sally prepares her best living room impression for Willie. |\n| `Cecil_Sally_Cecil_Confides_In_Sally.mp3` | **\"Cecil Confides in Sally\"** | **1930-11-03** | Cecil seeks advice about his upcoming social engagement. |\n| `Cecil_Sally_Loves_Me_Loves_Me_Not.mp3` | **\"Loves Me, Loves Me Not\"** | **1930-11-04** | Evening stroll disputes and humorous pet dilemmas. |\n| `Cecil_Sally_Thinking_Arrested_Rewarded.mp3` | **\"The Surprise Reward at the Boarding House\"** | **1930-11-05** | Boarding house dining room confusion turns into a cash reward. |\n"
